message: "If you use this preprint, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Geometry, Effort Metrics, and Holonomy in AI Reasoning Systems"
version: "1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hedling"
    given-names: "Borealis S."
    orcid: "0009-0004-7968-5707"
abstract: >
  This preprint formalizes Voronoi partitioning, effort-weighted geodesics, and
  holonomy-driven path dependence, demonstrating their relevance to modern AI
  reasoning systems. Embedding-space partitioning corresponds to Voronoi
  geometry, transition likelihoods induce an effort metric on semantic
  manifolds, and recurrent or transformer-style state evolution exhibits
  holonomy-like path dependence. The work provides a mathematically defensible
  foundation for analyzing AI behavior using tools from metric geometry,
  optimization, and differential topology.
keywords:
  - Voronoi geometry
  - effort metrics
  - holonomy
  - AI reasoning
  - NDH-Research-Pilot
  - differential topology
  - metric geometry
